msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2145
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:454
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I'm collecting used magic lamps, but I don't have any money.\nI'll trade you some of these pretty stones for the lamps, though."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2146
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:455
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Thanks for the lamp!\nHere are your stones."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2147
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:456
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "High Detail is only available with 32MB of RAM or greater."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2148
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npctext.txt.py:519
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Not Used"
msgstr "Not Used"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2150
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "This will sound odd, but bear with me, heroes. The name’s Verdant, and I am a time traveler. Something rather dire has occurred and I need your help. Actually, the world needs your help. I am but a messenger… and the probable cause of all the trouble, but that’s really not what’s important here. \nWhat is important is that there is this clandestine scholar consortium. It has no name for it should not be spoken of, and hence has no need for one. We are a group of mages who researched the intricacies of time travel for the purpose of documenting the history of our world. Pure, untainted, unbiased. Something humans entangled in their affairs and fettered by political agendas are obviously incapable of doing. As the saying goes, ‘Winners write history’. And hence, we’ve mastered the art of time travel to witness the history and document it objectively, straighten out the mangled facts, uncover the truth buried beneath convenient lies.\nIt’s been working out great, our archives grow with each excursion, but this time, a little something went… a little wrong."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2151
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "See, personally, I always found it disappointing how all the chronicles detail the lives of kings, queens, and other politicians. How they say, ‘and Queen Whatever knighted her heroes’. I don’t want to read about that, I want to read about the heroes. I want to know about mires they’ve trudged through, about the miles they’ve traversed, about the riches they hauled, and the little folk they’ve saved. \nSo I’ve taken it upon myself to write a chronicle that has all of it and more. I’ve chosen three groups of heroes whose deeds saved countless lives, and I’ve attuned my magic to visit them all at the very beginnings of their journeys. I meant to get to know them, understand where they come from, see the world through their eyes, breathe in the scent of their sweat and blood. Yes, literally, don’t be squeamish, it won’t do you much good in your line of work..."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2152
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "...Anyway, something went wrong with the ritual, some malfunction or other and, uh, well. I seem to have erased a group of heroes from existence. Or, alternatively, I’ve booted them to another existence, century, or era. Fingers crossed for the booting. Then, well, I’ve tried to fix it and the same thing kind of sort of happened to the second hero group. Before you ask – yes, you’re the third. No, you’re not getting booted or existentially eradicated. *Verdant glances over to a book she’s holding* Probably. As long as the same can be said for all of your organs, we should be good."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2153
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "What I need you to do is really rather simple in concept. Basically, I know you’re capable of saving the world, so I will need you to do it a few more times. Just three times total, don’t worry! With the other two groups of heroes currently or permanently indisposed, you’ve got to pick up the slack or things will get really messed up. I mean, really: the history will rewrite itself, and, given the scope of changes and the amount of lives affected, who knows. The history might just say ‘Enough is enough!’ and explode everything. A wild, yet educated, guess. So you see the problem.\nOh, you didn’t know you were heroes? Right, right, I tend to forget how stable-timed people operate and think. Of course. Well, yes, welcome to the hero-dom. You can try to escape your path, but in all honesty, it will be much easier to just get the world saving done.\nPersonally, I think I actually love this idea. It may sound cold, but I can’t help it, heroes are my weakness. And three time world-savers? I’m about to melt on the spot. Mrrrau! A silver lining, you may call it, yeah?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2154
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "To travel through time and step onto the paths meant to be traversed by other heroes, you will need to use dimension doors present in areas infused with magic. Fear not, they're safe. Somewhat.\nYou'll find one of them in Murmurwoods, another in Dragonsand, and, if I recall correctly, one more awaits on the Evenmorn Island. There could be more. Or not. Who knows? Either way, once you find your door, you can activate it by casting the Town Portal spell nearby. There's also the option of finding Dimension Door scrolls rolling around with other junk at some stores. I think most folks take them for dicey cooking recipes, so ask for those.\nNo need to rush, by the way. The Universe is slow in restructuring itself and acting on the changes made to the fabric of time, but do try to get it all done before you get old, aye?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2155
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "This one's lovely if you like colors. I mean, fiery red, sky blue, earthly brown, sea emerald. Haha. Yeah, well, the elements are everywhere here, quite in your face. They... overflowed, you could say. It's kind of a crisis really. Either way, you would take the role of caravan guards, but worry not - caravan's done riding, no boring trips. You can rob what's left, sell it to the adorable lizards inhabiting the isle, and then get on with more interesting heroics. Please do. Mmmm... heroics. Yesss. Oh, and they even have unicorns there! Sadly, you may need to kill them. They're a little bit on the vicious side. Rrrawr."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2156
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Oh this one is special. You get to be LORDS. Hear me? LORDS. That sounds so distinguished, don't you want to be LORDS? Ha. But to get that swell title, you must first win a scavenger hunt on a little isle. It's no biggie, there's hardly any competition. I mean it - don't think to wait it out and let someone else win to be free from that little prison. It's not going to happen. Win it and then you're home - ruling a small patch of land sitting right between two warring kingdoms who each want a piece of said land. Well, the whole of it, really. Fun. But hey, you get to call yourself LORDS. Who cares about the rest?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2157
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "This one's simple. You're a bunch of happy kids saved by a nice warlock fellow, spent your lives training, now all grown up and ready to roll. No need for a heavy roleplay, just don't be jerks. Go around, slap some goblins, squash a spider or two, poke a devil. Umm... I mean, an apprentice wizard, yes. No devils anywhere, forget the devils. I don't think I should be telling you things about your future. Well, their future. But also your future now. You know what I mean. From zero to hero, take your time, enjoy the views... once you find a vantage point free of death. Which is not going to be easy. This land is swarming with killey things. Seriously. I love it."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2158
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Good news: the whole hero-extinction mess wasn’t just my fault. Bad news: the whole hero-extinction mess wasn’t just my fault. In other news: there’s a Runaway Chaos that’s causing trouble and it must be caught and contained! More literally than one might like.\nI won’t get into the technical details, because the more I’d say, the less you’d understand – it’s perfectly normal, not a slight against your wits in the slightest. But in the simplest terms, imagine there’s something we’ll call a Chaos Matter, it’s the force of Chaos in the universe. Entropy and all that. And from this matter, a bit… fell off, let’s say, and began causing unpredictable trouble. And though you may think – but that’s what chaos ought to be! Chaotic! Let me treat you with a slogan – In every Chaos there is Order, in every Order there is Chaos. \nThe Runaway Chaos is the aforementioned bit. It attached to my spells and made them backfire horribly, as you well know. You have to go to the Controlled Breach, capture the Runaway Chaos, and return it to the uh… Uneasy Origin Matter. Yes, I made that name up, but no sane person can memorize the one we use to describe it in the consortium without hearing it a hundred times over."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2159
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The Controlled Breach is a place the consortium has created where it’s possible to see and interact with the Runaway Chaos, and through which the Uneasy Origin Matter can be reached. It’s an artificial realm-esque area where matters *Verdant snickers* can be safely handled without jeopardizing any real world places. \nRuins of Escaton's Crystal should be enough magic-filled to allow our old friend - town portal spell - teleport you there.\nOnce there, all you need to do is find the Runaway Chaos and return it to the Uneasy Origin Matter. What can you expect on the way? Aye, this even I cannot tell you. Since it’s a result of a time anomaly, we have obviously never seen it before. \nWhat will happen to you after you go in and leave?\nWell, um. Let’s not overthink things. I’m sure it’s going to be fun, though!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2160
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I have to figure out the exact cause of this whole timeline kerfuffle. There might be some more anomalies that I’ve missed. You’ve helped me a bunch already, but would you mind terribly if I called on you again at some point? I mean, you’re face-deep in this mess as it is and it’s not like you’re getting out of it anytime *Verdant snickers* soon. Might as well keep helping me, right?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2161
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Nifty gizmo, isn’t it? This gem will let us speak wherever and whenever. But, eh, as always there’s a but. The thing is quite unstable and will need to recharge after each contact we make. To put it simply, it absorbs energy from the air around it. You can either give it a few days or jump into the time-travel door for an instant recharge. Ever wondered why you come out of those with your hair standing straight in all directions? Now you know. Energy. Tons of it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2162
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "(Charged connector stone will heal you up once per day.)"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2163
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I’m glad you asked, this whole conundrum is making it rather difficult for me to sleep. I could pretend it’s the worry over the poor goobers I’ve punted out of our realm, existence, time, or whatnot that’s keeping me awake, but I’ve always been a big fan of truth telling. Lies are so much hassle to keep track of, aren’t they?\nBasically, I don’t much care about the scrubs I’ve sent away, but I do care an awful lot about the heroes snoozing within them. And I want those heroes back, and I want to put them in another time of trouble to witness their glory and maybe save a life or two while we’re at it. Hence I’ve been hard at work locating the two missing groups. But to make it happen in a reasonable amount of time, I will need your help."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2164
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You could ask, what value does time hold to a time traveler? And hasn’t the other heroes’ suffering has already begun – or, in fact, ended centuries ago, should they have found themselves in another period? And to that I’ll tell you: stop over thinking things. Trying to make sense of it all will just give you a headache. A rookie mistake of anyone dealing with paradox-prone situations.\nLook at it this way – we’re living in dangerous times. As all times are, really, so it’s not like we can hide elsewhen. *Verdant shrugs.* And so it’s not out of the realm of possibility that a dragon will eat me tomorrow, or the day after, and cut my work time short. It would be deeply troubling and unfortunate given that I’m also involved in other matters of great importance, but the point is – it could happen. I don’t know what awaits me in this timeline, provided I stay here, since I’ve never been here and now before… I think. Oh gods, now I’m doing it. Stop it, woman! *Verdant slaps her left ear as if she wanted the paradox musings to fall out of the right one.*\nAnyway, what I need you to do is help me build a Telelocator. Doing that will increase the chance of my finishing the task before I become a dragon snack.”"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2165
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "There’s two things to know here.\nOne: I cannot return the lost heroes to their own respective timelines as I’ve already attuned you to their paths. We’ll have to move them somewhen else or the universe could get really huffy and we would really not want that. If we plop them in some random, nicely troubled time and place they will start their own new paths, and all will be good.\n\nTwo: to commence said plopping, we must first locate the poor goobers. That can be accomplished by building a device we call the Telelocator. That’s where you come in.\nFirst things first, we need a Rod. Not just any rod, but a special rod of an infused metal. There’s a clan of Duergars dwelling near Alvar who dabble with this kind of ore. I’m sure they’ll have a rod somewhere around their complex, what half-competent blacksmith wouldn’t have one? I’d suggest to simply purchase it, but I’ve heard them Duergars are rather grumpy. And by grumpy I mean they would rather lodge an axe in your head than barter.\n"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2166
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "How’s the Rod expedition going? No, I cannot use a wooden stick instead, stop asking or I’ll get one and use it for another purpose next time you do. Ass-whooping in the purpose, in case there was any doubt."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2167
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Brilliant. This is a wonderful rod. Have you run your hand over it? Try it! Bzzt. Bzzt! Fun, isn’t it? Next we’ll need a Guiding Gem."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2168
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Acquire an Infused Metal Rod for Verdant to serve as a base of the Telelocator. She said Duergars of Alvar may own a few."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2169
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "There is no such thing as a Guiding Gem, obviously, we have to make one. I will need a large round crystal for this. LARGE. ROUND. And I mean, *SERIOUSLY ROUND*. None of that shady vendor garbage. If the stream gets skewed due to an uneven orb shape I might get a nosebleed of the century when I use the Telelocator. I’ve already sprayed the halls for the century two centuries back, and also for the one six from now, and I’m definitely not into repeating that experience.\nSo yes, round please. I’ve asked around and been told that the dwarves of the Stone City might have something like that stashed away. They sure love their crystals and when it comes to classy stone cutting they have no equals.\nIs it possible you will have to steal it? Please, we are living in a world of wonders. Dragons, Unicorns, talking trees, might and magic. Of course it’s possible, what sort of a dumb question is that?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2170
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The dwarves are generally a very friendly folk. If they get mad at you, just bolt and give them a moment to cool off while firmly out of their sight. Or learn to be sneaky and don’t get caught in the first place. I’d advise the latter, but I won’t be surprised if you just go and slaughter everyone instead. You wouldn’t believe the things some world-saving heroes liked to do. *Verdant rolls her eyes, but a corner of her lips twitches in a way that makes you wonder if she doesn’t appreciate an occasional anti-hero spicing up her chronicles.*"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2171
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Great, this is beautiful. So smooth… I could just sit and pet it for hours. Which I might well do until you return with the Wisp Wrappings, as there’s little progress to be made meanwhile."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2172
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Acquire a Large Seriously Round Crystal for Verdant’s Telelocator. One could possibly be found in the Stone City located in Barrow Downs."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2173
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Good, good, we almost have our thing pieced together. To attach the gem to the rod I need one more thing – Wisp Wrappings. It’s basically bandages, but infused with a strong spiritual essence. That can only happen if they touched the “flesh” of an undead and have spent some time being filled with a strong spiritual presence.\nI know just the place to look for such a thing. Near the Castle Ironfist you will find a place that used to belong to a wizard named Corlagon. That hole is just swarming with all sorts of undead. If a piece of cloth ever fell off one of them, it will be perfect. Those ghosts there seem to be very… bed-sheety. So I wouldn’t be at all surprised if the entire area was littered with bits that tore off them while they flew around the corridors.\nWhat? You don’t know what bed sheets are? You poor things! Grab yourself a ghost carcass in the Estate then and line your bed with it next time. You’ll thank me!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2174
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Don’t tell me not one of those ghosts has ever ran into a sharp nail sticking out of the wall or another?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2175
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Lovely, that’s exactly what I needed. Mmm… and it smells delicious too. If you can look past the odor of death and rotting meat. Here try it, look for that subtle note in the background. Oh, come on! Why does no one ever want to share the simple pleasures with me? *Verdant pouts* Fine, business then. We need to enchant the rod and the gem now."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2176
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Acquire Wisp Wrappings for Verdant’s Telelocator. She suggested searching for some in the Corlagon’s Estate near Castle Ironfist."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2177
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Infusing the Guiding Gem might turn out to be an affair more expensive than dangerous. I’d love to reimburse you but, alas, I don’t have any currency valid in this here time period. In the place I’ve last visited with an intention to buy things they stopped trading in gold. *Verdant shows you a bunch of useless paper scraps* You could get a horse for this. Fun, no?\nWhat I need right now are gems – a great variety of gems. Bring me one of %s. I need to powder them and experiment to find the right dust combination that will properly attune the Guiding Gem to the realms."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2178
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Acquire %s for Verdant’s Telelocator. They can be found all over the world and bought from various merchants."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2179
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I really hope you like collecting things. Do not tell me otherwise, let me stay blissfully happy for you!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2180
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Well, this is %s, I still need %s."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2181
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Oh, aren’t these just gorgeous? It’s almost a shame to turn them to dust… I wonder if there could be another way---OKAY, FINE I’LL DO IT! No need for these death stares, what are you, gorgons? *Verdant mumbles something under her breath.*"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2182
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The rod can be enchanted with just a little bit of leg work. You will need to drop by the four Elemental Planes, but before you panic – don’t. What I need can be found near the very entrance of each of them.\nAll you need to do is go inside, boink the frame with a sword or whatever you have at hand, and pick up what falls off. These metal structures are surprisingly soft, it’s the rampaging elemental middle that’s holding it all together and actually shaping the thing. Who’d have guessed, huh? You may even just find some chippings lying around to save you the hassle. Seriously, an angry cat could probably bite one off.\nEither way, bring me four of the chippings and I’ll melt them into the rod to give it the much needed power."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2183
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Acquire Fire Portal Chipping, Water Portal Chipping, Earth Portal Chipping, and Air Portal Chipping for Verdant’s Telelocator. They can be found inside the Elemental Planes near the entrance portal."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2184
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You can try to bite the frames if you want, too. If a cat can do it so can you. But remember – it must be the frame inside the realm. The outer ones are actually quite tough and would definitely chip your teeth instead. Don’t ask me why that’s so, I didn’t make them."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2185
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You've acquired %s Chipping!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2186
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Okay, give me these and let’s see how that works out."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2187
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Wonderful, gorgeous, beautiful. Now that we have this puppy in one piece and magical enough, on top of being attuned to the realms, we need to do one more thing before I activate it. Well, one-ish. We need to attune it to the heroic spirits, traits found in heroes, kindred souls of valiance, call it however you want. Long story short, I need you to hold it and let it become drunk with your awesomeness. The problematic part may be, you need to actually be awesome for the device to want to drink from you.\nLuckily, it doesn’t need to feed on just one person. No, it won’t literally suck the thing out of you! Seriously? I’m being metaphorical. Why would I want to break you… *Verdant sighs and shakes her head.* Telelocator needs to feel Might, Endurance, Accuracy, Intellect, Personality, and Luck. If you feel strong at one of them, come forth, take it, and close your eyes. Tell it, in your mind, about your valor. If it deems you worthy and absorbs your essence – NOT by taking it away, I SWEAR – the Guiding Gem will glow."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2188
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid " [insufficient] Harder! Try to squeeze it maybe?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2189
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "*The Telelocator brightens up. Verdant whispers something under her breath with her eyes following every twitch of your muscles.*"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2190
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid " [insufficient] Maybe if you first do a few rounds up and down the stairs?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2191
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "*The Telelocator brightens up.* I wish I could ‘attune’ myself to you too. I’m out of breath after a ten seconds run. Heck, I’m out of breath just talking about it. *Verdant pants.*"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2192
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid " [insufficient] Try squinting. More. More! Close your eyes! Aim with your mind alone! Eh. Still nothing."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2193
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "*The Telelocator brightens up.* Can you hunt me a deer for dinner? I’ve been eating local shrooms for too many days already. Bleh."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2194
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid " [insufficient] Did it ask you a riddle or something? If so, do tell, I’m curious if I’d get it right."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2195
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "*The Telelocator brightens up.* Sweet. You know, we should meet for a round of Ugili Duli once. It’s a fascinating game, but nobody around seems to even get the rules. Much less pose a challenge!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2196
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid " [insufficient] Don’t worry, I personally think you’re very, very charming and… personable. Mrrr…"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2197
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "*The Telelocator brightens up.* Then the gizmo and I are in agreement."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2198
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid " [insufficient] How often do you step in poop? I find that’s a good measure of how badly the world hates you. Once you get to less than twice a day give it another go."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2199
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "*The Telelocator brightens up.* It’s our lucky day! The fortune smiles on us today! Hm. I had more cliches ready for this one, but they fled my mind. I guess you really *are* lucky."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2200
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Pass the test Might (70) to attune the Telelocator.\nPass the test Endurance (70) to attune the Telelocator.\nPass the test Accuracy (70) to attune the Telelocator.\nPass the test Intellect (70) to attune the Telelocator.\nPass the test Personality (70) to attune the Telelocator.\nPass the test Luck (70) to attune the Telelocator"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2201
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "We’re almost there. I can nearly hear the desperate cries for help from our punted friends! Provided they still actually exist somewhere and haven’t been straight out erased from everywhere… let’s stick to nearly hearing their cries, aye?\nNow this may be a toughie. To activate the Telelocator I will need a lot of power. Not a fancy power core kind of power, but still. Ten Philosopher Stones is what we’re looking for here. Once you bring them to me, we can finally use the thing! I’m getting excited."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2202
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "May I suggest an alchemy lab heist? Desperate times desperate measures and all that."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2203
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Well, %s more stones left."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2204
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Brilliant. No more talk. Let’s go."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2205
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Acquire 10 Philosopher Stones to activate the Telelocator."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2206
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "*Verdant performs quite a lengthy ritual to activate the Telelocator, and just when you begin to worry that it may not work after all this work, the device beams up and the sorceress opens her eyes wide. She’s looking straight at you, but her gaze is absent, as she’s not seeing you, but things from realms, or times, far away or long time away from here and now. Then, she speaks, strangely mechanically.”\nTargets found. Realms: Attuned. Time: Attuned.\nWorld: Ashan. Year: 1923\nTargets’ Status: Incapacitated and confused. Targets’ predicted remaining lifespan: Eleven thousand and sixty six days.\nRealms: Detached. Time: Detached.\n*Verdant opens her eyes with a gasp.*\nAw, crap."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2207
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Yes, we can do it. I don’t know how much you’ve heard, but I know exactly how to bring the lost heroes back into our world and place them in a more fair predicament. I will need some gruesome stuff for that. It’s all about sacrifice and suffering now, you know. Also, do make haste as always, but don’t worry about time too much. Telelocator has detached both timelines so as long as I’m alive and the universe doesn’t backflip, the heroes can be saved.\nI will need you to bring me 5 Will’o’Wisp Hearts, 5 Wolf Eyes, 3 Phoenix Feathers, a vial of Troll Blood, a vial of Gog Blood, 2 Dragon’s Eyes, and a Focal Ring.\nThen I will… Let’s not think or talk about it right now. Go, let’s save those Goobers so they can become the heroes we all know they can be!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2208
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "That’s not enough murder. Get on it, aye? Trust me, I’m getting the short end of the stick here…"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2209
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "This is %s, fine. "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2210
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Need %s more. "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2211
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "And also, %s "
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2212
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I have to say, I was kind of sort of hoping you might not be back… Eech! Yes, I do have to mash it all together and drink it. In theory, so do you each time you drink this or that potion, but trust me, it’s a whole different story when you just straight out… mash it… no boiling… no magic. *Verdant closes her eyes and inhales sharply.* I feel sick and filthy already. Can you mix it for me at least? Leave the feather shafts out…"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2213
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "With *pleasure*?! What is that supposed to mean?! Some heroes you are! *She crosses her arms on her chest and kicks a pot your way. You mix the ingredients together and offer the sorceress the resulting goop. It is, indeed, a sight to behold… right before barfing.*\nHere it goes. *It takes Verdant a good while to actually do as she must, but eventually she proves her dedication to the cause and downs the mixture.*"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2214
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Well, the ring seemed stuck in my throat for a moment, but I think it passed through. WHO made this recipe? *She glares at a book lying to the side then takes the device and begins to activate it again. The mechanical voice is back.*\nTargets found. Realms: Attuned. Time: Attuned.\nTargets: Attuned. Captured. Removed. Resummoned. Placed. Detached. \nWorld: Enroth Year: 1176. Continent: Vori.\n*The channeling is over and Verdant opens her eyes smiling at you.*"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2215
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "All in all, that was pretty hero-efficient, I must say. One group for the prize of three and then two to spare for future or past catastrophes. Though with all of them placed in the same spot it might be a bit of a hero-oversaturation there. On the other hand, maybe they’ll fall in love and multiply eventually? If you ask me, I think the world needs all the heroes it can get. Yes, I *know* I can just check, don’t be such a buzz kill!\nBut great job, I mean it. Saving heroes, saving worlds, I might be falling in love with you myself. Just kidding, that’s a done deal. It was love at first sight!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2216
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Acquire 10 5 Will’o’Wisp Hearts, 5 Wolf Eyes, 3 Phoenix Feathers, a vial of troll Blood, a vial of Gog Blood, 2 Dragon’s Eyes, and a Focal Ring to bring back the lost heroes."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2217
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Other heroes#Help the Goobers#Telelocator#Infused metal rod#Guiding gem#Wisp wrappings#Telelocator parts#Enchant the Gem#Enchant the Rod#Attune the Telelocator#Attune #Activate the Telelocator#Activate!#Save the Goobers!#Mix the potion#...#Dimensionally displaced goobers"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2219
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You see it about in field and town,\nIt cannot get up,\nBut will often fall down."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2220
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "rain"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2221
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The strongest chains will not bind it,\nditch and rampart will not slow it down.\nA thousand soldiers cannot beat it,\nit can knock down trees with a single push."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2222
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "wind"
msgstr "ウインド"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2223
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "An untiring servant it is,\ncarrying loads across muddy earth.\nBut one thing that cannot be forced,\nis a return to the place of its birth."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2224
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "river"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2225
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "With sharp edged wit,\nAnd pointed poise,\nIt can settle disputes,\nWithout a noise."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2226
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "sword"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2227
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It is too much for one.\nTwo it is meant for.\nBut it no longer exists,\nWhen the two become more."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2228
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "secret"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2229
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "This old one runs forever,\nBut never moves at all.\nHe has not lungs, nor throat,\nStill, a mighty roaring call."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2230
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "waterfall"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2231
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It can move over water,\nBut cannot fly.\nIt can move under water,\nBut stay quite dry."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2232
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "shadow"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2233
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "It doesn't live with in a house,\nNor does it live without.\nMost will use it when they come in,\nAnd again when they go out."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2234
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "door"
msgstr "扉"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2235
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "A shimmering field that reaches far.\nYet it has no tracks,\nAnd is crossed without paths."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2236
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "ocean"
msgstr "Ocean"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2237
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "This engulfing thing,\nis strange indeed.\nThe greater it grows,\nthe less you see."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2238
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "darkness"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2239
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "When it comes in,\nFrom sea to shore,\nTwenty paces you'll see,\nNo less, no more."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2240
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "fog"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2242
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "%s, friend! You are here, I'm so glad to meet you."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2243
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I thought I'm lost here, nice to see you again."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2244
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "At least one familiar face amongst this madness, %s!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2245
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Finally, friends!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2246
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Who are you? Another horror of this place? If not, let's stay together."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2247
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hello, live being."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2248
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "All the wizards around here have gone mad, but their golems are still functioning. The important part is, I don’t want to be here any longer than I absolutely have to."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2249
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Can you believe these swordsmen thought I was Prince Nicolai? Amazing. Anyway, at least it’s safe in here."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2250
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The area is swarming with fire elementals. I killed some, but they just keep on coming. Well, at least the fort is empty, so there’s that. Man, it’s so hot in here. Do you have any water? Anything liquid?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2251
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "These stinky hulks outside are about as friendly as they smell. I’ve snuck in here to wait for dawn to come, but it’s still dark outside and I’ve lost the track of time completely."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2252
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "This place is a madhouse! The thing we’re looking for – the Runaway Chaos – it’s not a living being. Think of a ghost or a spirit of some sort."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2253
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "This place… it sends shivers down my spine. It reminds me of Alvar, but we will find no elves here. The lights in the houses turn on and off, even though nobody is here. I think we should look for Runaway Chaos in one of the buildings."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2254
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Look, I found a diary of some poor sod. Or rather what remains of it. It seems someone got into the Breach long before us… if we can speak in terms of time around here at all. He wrote: “Everything in here is a reflection of things that happened, somewhere, somewhen. None of it is real, with the exception of the Personalities.” It looks like the poor fellow has failed to find a way out of here and began to lose his mind. The last pages are just filled with gibberish about some riddles."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2255
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My friends! I found it! The Runaway Chaos! Or maybe… maybe it found me? I don’t know, I don’t know, it all feels like a grand jest. It surrounded me with hellish creatures, monsters born of my nightmares. To scare me, perhaps, or just see what I would do. I fought to stay alive and it just laughed. As I say these words, I hear echoes of this screeching laughter piercing through my very skull. And when I finally fell to the ground, without a shred of power left to carry on, suddenly the nightmares… dissipated. Gone, every single one. But the wounds they left were real… and yet, when I looked down, there wasn’t a single cut. Only my torn clothes stood as proof that anything had happened at all.\nAnd then the being spoke to me, in a voice so calm, my own shivers ceased. “I will ask you riddles five,” it said, “Answer them to feel alive. Make a wish if you succeed, maybe then you shall be freed.” I did not know the answers. But it let me be. I don’t know why. Maybe it felt pity. Or maybe it merely wanted to let me rest before it returns to torment me once again."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2256
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Don't waste my time!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2257
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Never heard of it."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2258
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "What is this? A new shop?"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2259
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ah, I do love me some riddles. Tell me what this is:"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2260
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I remember one from my childhood:"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2261
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Sometimes you can find riddles in random books. Delightfully unepexected. Like this one:"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2262
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "This one was mumbled in a tavern by a drooling drunk. His last words, actually:"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2263
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Hmm, yes, that will do. It was fun picking your brain, very enjoyable indeed. A good time begs a good reward. Make a wish and I shall make it come true."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2264
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I don't know anymore."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2265
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Correct!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2266
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Not quite, friend, not quite."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2268
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Well, I have no skills to offer, but I'm good company!\nJust feed me and throw me a few gold pieces and I'll be happy to accompany you!"
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2269
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I'll happily join you for 200 gold and %17 percent of all the gold we find.\nI'll fix any weapon you ask me to while I work for you."
msgstr "I'll happily join you for 200 gold and %17 percent of all the gold we find.  I'll fix any weapon you ask me to while I work for you."

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2270
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I'm looking for work fixing armor.\nAll I charge is 200 gold to start and %17 percent of all the gold we find.\nYou won't regret hiring me!"
msgstr "I'm looking for work fixing armor.  All I charge is 200 gold to start and %17 percent of all the gold we find.  You won't regret hiring me!"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2271
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I can mend any broken magic item you have, unless it's a piece of armor or a weapon.\nMy rate is 400 gold to start plus %17 percent of all the gold we find."
msgstr "I can mend any broken magic item you have, unless it's a piece of armor or a weapon.  My rate is 400 gold to start plus %17 percent of all the gold we find."

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2272
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I studied under Lord Newton in Mist for eight years to learn to tell one magic item from another.\nI'll work for you for 500 gold to start, plus a %17 percent share of all the gold we find."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2273
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I know shortcuts and back roads throughout Enroth.\nI'll be your guide for a mere 100 gold to start and a %17 percent share of all the gold we find."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2274
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I know shortcuts and back roads throughout Enroth.\nI'll be your guide for 200 gold to start, plus a %17 percent share of the gold we find."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2275
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I know shortcuts and back roads throughout Enroth.\nI'll be your guide for a mere 300 gold to start, plus a %17 percent share of the gold we find."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2276
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Uh, Ya.\nI can uh, you know, work.\nOn a boat.\nI'll help get you places quicker.\nWith me, I can get you across the sea two days faster than normal.Uh, I uh, want oh, let's see, 100 gold to start, and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "Uh, Ya.  I can uh, you know, work.  On a boat.  I'll help get you places quicker.  With me, I can get you across the sea two days faster than normal.  Uh, I uh, want oh, let's see, 100 gold to start, and %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2277
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I've spent quite some time putting together accurate charts of the waters surrounding our continent.\nWith my charts and my skill, I can get you across water three days faster than normal.\nI charge 200 gold to start, plus %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "I've spent quite some time putting together accurate charts of the waters surrounding our continent.  With my charts and my skill, I can get you across water three days faster than normal.  I charge 200 gold to start, plus %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2278
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I can travel with you, my children, for an initial donation of 500 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find to my church.\nOnce per day I'll be able to heal you of all your wounds, short of death."
msgstr "I can travel with you, my children, for an initial donation of 500 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find to my church.  Once per day I'll be able to heal you of all your wounds, short of death."

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2279
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "As an expert healer, I can heal your wounds and many other conditions (but not death or turned to stone) once per day.\nAll I require is a donation of 2000 to my church and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "As an expert healer, I can heal your wounds and many other conditions (but not death or turned to stone) once per day.  All I require is a donation of 2000 to my church and %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2280
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "As a master healer, my services are in demand by many, but my power to magically heal only works but once per day.\nI can heal everything but eradication, and require a modest initial donation of 5000 gold to my temple and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "As a master healer, my services are in demand by many, but my power to magically heal only works but once per day.  I can heal everything but eradication, and require a modest initial donation of 5000 gold to my temple and %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2281
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I can help you to interpret and understand what you see as you travel. I think my advice will increase your overall experience.\nI must charge 300 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find for my services, however."
msgstr "I can help you to interpret and understand what you see as you travel. I think my advice will increase your overall experience.  I must charge 300 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find for my services, however."

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2282
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I can help you to interpret and understand what you see as you travel. I think my advice will increase your overall experience.\nI must charge 700 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find for my\nservices, however."
msgstr "I can help you to interpret and understand what you see as you travel. I think my advice will increase your overall experience.  I must charge 700 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find for my  services, however."

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2283
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Everyone benefits from good advice, and my advice on weapons and combat is amongst the best.\nDuring battle, my direction will improve your skill at arms.\nI charge but 300 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "Everyone benefits from good advice, and my advice on weapons and combat is amongst the best.  During battle, my direction will improve your skill at arms.  I charge but 300 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2284
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Everyone benefits from good advice, and my advice on weapons and combat is the best.\nDuring battle, my direction will significantly improve your skill at arms.\nI charge but 400 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "Everyone benefits from good advice, and my advice on weapons and combat is the best.  During battle, my direction will significantly improve your skill at arms.  I charge but 400 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2285
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I can lend a little magic to boost your spell skills and ease your magical burden for 500 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2286
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I can lend a good deal of magic to magnify your spell skills for 1000 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2287
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I can lend my considerable magic reserves to sharply increase your spell skills and effects for the low, low price of 2000 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2288
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Sometimes, people have trouble bargaining in their own behalf.\nI'll be happy to give you advice to better the prices you receive while bargaining with Merchants.\nAll I ask is 100 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "Sometimes, people have trouble bargaining in their own behalf.  I'll be happy to give you advice to better the prices you receive while bargaining with Merchants.  All I ask is 100 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2289
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "As a long time member of the Merchant's Guild, and a former rug Merchant myself, I know all the tricks of the trade like the back of my hand.\nI can give you advice while bargaining with other Merchants to improve the prices you get.\nMy fee is but 200 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "As a long time member of the Merchant's Guild, and a former rug merchant myself, I know all the tricks of the trade like the back of my hand.  I can give you advice while bargaining with other Merchants to improve the prices you get.  My fee is but 200 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2290
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My eyes are sharp, and my voice is loud.\nI can alert you to danger before it strikes.\nMay save your life…And all I need is 300 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "My eyes are sharp, and my voice is loud.  I can alert you to danger before it strikes.  May save your life�And all I need is 300 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2291
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I've spent my life in and around courts and bureaucracies, and I know how to make people more…sympathetic to a cause.\nHire me, and I'll do the same for you.\n200 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2292
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I've spent my life in and around courts and bureaucracies, and I know how to make people more…sympathetic to a cause.\nHire me, and I'll do the same for you.\n300 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2293
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I know a thing or two about fixing tools and whatnot.\nI also know about locks.\nI can help you pick them if you hire me for 200 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "I know a thing or two about fixing tools and whatnot.  I also know about locks.  I can help you pick them if you hire me for 200 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2294
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Locksmithing is a difficult thing to learn, and you need a professional with you to help you handle the toughest locks.\nI can work for you for 300 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "Locksmithing is a difficult thing to learn, and you need a professional with you to help you handle the toughest locks.  I can work for you for 300 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2295
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "The gods favor drunks, children and fools.\nWell, I'm a fool!\nTake me with you and maybe the gods will favor you too.\nAll I want is 100 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find"
msgstr "The gods favor drunks, children and fools.  Well, I'm a fool!  Take me with you and maybe the gods will favor you too.  All I want is 100 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2296
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "People say Chimney Sweeps are lucky.\nI don't know about that– sweeping chimneys is hard work!\nBut if you want, you could hire me for 200 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find..\nMaybe I'll bring you good luck."
msgstr "People say Chimney Sweeps are lucky.  I don't know about that� sweeping chimneys is hard work!  But if you want, you could hire me for 200 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find..  Maybe I'll bring you good luck."

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2297
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "If you need someone to carry some traveller's comforts, like tents and cooking gear, I'm your man!\nAll I want is 100 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "If you need someone to carry some traveller's comforts, like tents and cooking gear, I'm your man!  All I want is 100 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2298
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "For 200 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find, I'll organize all your camping needs and carry your gear.\nI think you'll find me well worth the price!"
msgstr "For 200 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find, I'll organize all your camping needs and carry your gear.  I think you'll find me well worth the price!"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2299
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "For 500 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find I'll organize your finances and check all the coins you find for rarity.\nI can usually increase a client's wealth by 5 percent."
msgstr "For 500 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find I'll organize your finances and check all the coins you find for rarity.  I can usually increase a client's wealth by 5 percent."

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2300
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "For 1000 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find I'll organize your finances and check all the coins you find for rarity.\nI can usually increase a client's wealth by 10 percent."
msgstr "For 1000 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find I'll organize your finances and check all the coins you find for rarity.  I can usually increase a client's wealth by 10 percent."

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2301
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ever want your own personal cook?\nFor 300 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find, I'll carry extra food and prepare your meals for myself and the four of you.\nYou won't be sorry– everyone loves my cooking!"
msgstr "Ever want your own personal cook?  For 300 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find, I'll carry extra food and prepare your meals for myself and the four of you.  You won't be sorry� everyone loves my cooking!"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2302
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I have studied in the finest cooking schools in Enroth, and I am willing to prepare your meals for a paltry 400 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2303
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I can see you know little about handling horses and getting the most out of them.\nI'll be happy to take care of any horses you use when you rent horses at the stables.\nYou'll get to your destination faster with my help.\nAll I want is 100 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "I can see you know little about handling horses and getting the most out of them.  I'll be happy to take care of any horses you use when you rent horses at the stables.  You'll get to your destination faster with my help.  All I want is 100 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2304
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My reputation as a famous musician follows me wherever I go.\nIf I'm with you, I'm sure some of my reputation will rub off on you.\nI only need 1000 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find for living expenses."
msgstr "My reputation as a famous musician follows me wherever I go.  If I'm with you, I'm sure some of my reputation will rub off on you.  I only need 1000 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find for living expenses."

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2305
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Dangerous Sorcerers abound throughout the land of Enroth.\nMost use spells that do some sort of elemental damage, like fire or lightning.\nI know a spell that will protect you from these elements, and I can keep it going all the time.\nI'll cast it for you if you take me along.\nAll I want is 1000 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2306
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "For 200 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find, I can cast the Wizard Eye spell at expert level constantly."
msgstr "For 200 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find, I can cast the Wizard Eye spell at expert level constantly."

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2307
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ever want to fly?\nTake me with you and I can cast the Fly spell on you once a day.\nAll I ask is 2000 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find.\nCheap, huh?"
msgstr "Ever want to fly?  Take me with you and I can cast the Fly spell on you once a day.  All I ask is 2000 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find.  Cheap, huh?"

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2308
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Ancient prophets claimed the power to walk on water, and I've rediscovered their secret.\nOnce per day I can cast the Water Walk spell on you and everyone with you.\nMy rate is 1000 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "Ancient prophets claimed the power to walk on water, and I've rediscovered their secret.  Once per day I can cast the Water Walk spell on you and everyone with you.  My rate is 1000 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2309
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "There are spells that duplicate some of the natural magical features of Enroth.\nOne of those, Town Portal, I've learned to cast at master level.\nI'll\ncast it for you up to once per day if you hire me.\nMy price is 2000 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2310
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "For a donation of 200 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find to my temple, I'll travel with you and cast the Bless spell once per day."
msgstr "For a donation of 200 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find to my temple, I'll travel with you and cast the Bless spell once per day."

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2311
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "All armies travelling in style bring a piper along to inspire them to heroic deeds during combat.\nEven small groups like your own can benefit.\nI'll travel with you for 300 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "All armies travelling in style bring a piper along to inspire them to heroic deeds during combat.  Even small groups like your own can benefit.  I'll travel with you for 300 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2312
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My experience in travelling the world can speed your journeys by a day whether you travel by land or by sea.\nAll I require is 100 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "My experience in travelling the world can speed your journeys by a day whether you travel by land or by sea.  All I require is 100 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2313
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Arrr.\nMy life as a freedom-loving sailor has taught me to travel quickly on the seas and count my gold well.\nBut I'm down on my luck these days, so I'll sign on with you for only 500 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "Arrr.  My life as a freedom-loving sailor has taught me to travel quickly on the seas and count my gold well.  But I'm down on my luck these days, so I'll sign on with you for only 500 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2314
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "All warriors need a squire to take care of their weapons and armor and back them up in battle.\nI'll be your squire for 600 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "All warriors need a squire to take care of their weapons and armor and back them up in battle.  I'll be your squire for 600 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2315
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Fortune is my business, and I can improve your fortunes for 400 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "Fortune is my business, and I can improve your fortunes for 400 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find.  "

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2316
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "My entire life has been spent on the road, and believe me when I say you gotta know how to travel and you gotta know how to deal.\nI can help you with both for 100 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "My entire life has been spent on the road, and believe me when I say you gotta know how to travel and you gotta know how to deal.  I can help you with both for 100 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2317
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Not everyone knows how to talk strangers into giving them what they want.\nI make it my specialty.\nBring me along and I'll use my skills to ease your way through society.\nMy rate is 500 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "Not everyone knows how to talk strangers into giving them what they want.  I make it my specialty.  Bring me along and I'll use my skills to ease your way through society.  My rate is 500 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2318
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Lots of people can be talked out of stuff they would never give up if they thought about it.\nThe trick is to talk fast and don't let them pause to consider what you're really saying.\nI'll stay with you and coach you on this valuable skill for only 200 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "Lots of people can be talked out of stuff they would never give up if they thought about it.  The trick is to talk fast and don't let them pause to consider what you're really saying.  I'll stay with you and coach you on this valuable skill for only 200 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2319
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Need traps disarmed?\nI've been doing it ever since I was released from jail three years ago.\nIf you need help, I'll come with you for free!\nI need the practice."
msgstr ""

#: mmmerge/Data/Text localization/LANG_NPCText.txt.py:2320
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "I don't have any skills to offer you, but if this will get me out of school and away from my chores, I'd love to follow you around!"
