#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:40
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npcprof.txt.py:40
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "My reputation as a famous musician follows me wherever I go.  If I'm with you, I'm sure some of my reputation will rub off on you.  I only need 1000 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find for living expenses."
msgstr "My reputation as a famous musician follows me wherever I go.  If I'm with you, I'm sure some of my reputation will rub off on you.  I only need 1000 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find for living expenses."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:40
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "I thought we had a deal!  You're just going to cast me aside like trash! How could you?"
msgstr "I thought we had a deal!  You're just going to cast me aside like trash! How could you?"

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:41
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Increases protection from air, earth, fire, water, body, and mind by 20 constantly.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."
msgstr "Increases protection from air, earth, fire, water, body, and mind by 20 constantly.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:41
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Dangerous Sorcerers abound throughout the land of Erathia.  Most use spells that do some sort of elemental damage, like fire or lightning.  Others use body or mind magic to assault their foes.  I know a spell that will help protect you from these, and I can keep it going all the time.  I'll cast it for you if you take me along.  All I want is 1000 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "Dangerous Sorcerers abound throughout the land of Erathia.  Most use spells that do some sort of elemental damage, like fire or lightning.  Others use body or mind magic to assault their foes.  I know a spell that will help protect you from these, and I can keep it going all the time.  I'll cast it for you if you take me along.  All I want is 1000 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:41
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Not afraid of hostile magic anymore eh?  Ok, your choice.  Don't say I didn't warn you!"
msgstr "Not afraid of hostile magic anymore eh?  Ok, your choice.  Don't say I didn't warn you!"

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:42
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npcprof.txt.py:42
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Keeps the Wizard Eye spell at expert ranking going at all times.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."
msgstr "Keeps the Wizard Eye spell at expert ranking going at all times.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:42
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npcprof.txt.py:42
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "For 200 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find, I can cast the Wizard Eye spell at expert level constantly."
msgstr "For 200 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find, I can cast the Wizard Eye spell at expert level constantly."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:42
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Even if you can cast Wizard eye on your own, keeping me around would save you the spell energy.  Did you think of that?"
msgstr "Even if you can cast Wizard eye on your own, keeping me around would save you the spell energy.  Did you think of that?"

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:43
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Wind Walk"
msgstr "Wind Walk"

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:43
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npcprof.txt.py:43
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Casts the Fly spell (duration 2 hours) once per day.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."
msgstr "Casts the Fly spell (duration 2 hours) once per day.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:43
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npcprof.txt.py:43
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Ever want to fly?  Take me with you and I can cast the Fly spell on you once a day.  All I ask is 2000 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find.  Cheap, huh?"
msgstr "Ever want to fly?  Take me with you and I can cast the Fly spell on you once a day.  All I ask is 2000 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find.  Cheap, huh?"

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:43
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "You're would give up the power of flight over a few measly gold pieces?  Think it through carefully, my friend."
msgstr "You're would give up the power of flight over a few measly gold pieces?  Think it through carefully, my friend."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:44
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Cross Water"
msgstr "Cross Water"

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:44
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npcprof.txt.py:44
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Casts the Water Walk spell (duration 3 hours) once per day.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."
msgstr "Casts the Water Walk spell (duration 3 hours) once per day.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:44
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npcprof.txt.py:44
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Ancient prophets claimed the power to walk on water, and I've rediscovered their secret.  Once per day I can cast the Water Walk spell on you and everyone with you.  My rate is 1000 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "Ancient prophets claimed the power to walk on water, and I've rediscovered their secret.  Once per day I can cast the Water Walk spell on you and everyone with you.  My rate is 1000 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:44
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "You're would give up the power to walk on water over a few measly gold pieces?  Think it through carefully, my friend."
msgstr "You're would give up the power to walk on water over a few measly gold pieces?  Think it through carefully, my friend."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:45
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Gate to Town"
msgstr "Gate to Town"

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:45
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npcprof.txt.py:45
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Casts the Town Portal spell at master ranking once per day.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."
msgstr "Casts the Town Portal spell at master ranking once per day.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:45
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "There are spells that duplicate some of the natural magical features of Erathia.  One of those, Town Portal, I've learned to cast at master level.  I'll  cast it for you up to once per day if you hire me.  My price is 2000 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "There are spells that duplicate some of the natural magical features of Erathia.  One of those, Town Portal, I've learned to cast at master level.  I'll  cast it for you up to once per day if you hire me.  My price is 2000 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:45
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "You're would give up the power to travel instantly for a few measly gold pieces?  Think it through carefully, my friend."
msgstr "You're would give up the power to travel instantly for a few measly gold pieces?  Think it through carefully, my friend."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:46
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Bless Party"
msgstr "Bless Party"

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:46
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npcprof.txt.py:46
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Casts the Bless spell (duration 2 hours) at master ranking once per day.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."
msgstr "Casts the Bless spell (duration 2 hours) at master ranking once per day.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:46
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npcprof.txt.py:46
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "For a donation of 200 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find to my temple, I'll travel with you and cast the Bless spell once per day."
msgstr "For a donation of 200 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find to my temple, I'll travel with you and cast the Bless spell once per day."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:46
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "I checked with the gods, and they said they would be angry with you if you dismissed me.  Just thought I would let you know…"
msgstr "I checked with the gods, and they said they would be angry with you if you dismissed me.  Just thought I would let you know�"

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:47
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Play Tune"
msgstr "Play Tune"

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:47
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npcprof.txt.py:47
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Casts the Heroism spell (duration 2 hours) at master ranking once per day.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."
msgstr "Casts the Heroism spell (duration 2 hours) at master ranking once per day.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:47
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npcprof.txt.py:47
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "All armies travelling in style bring a piper along to inspire them to heroic deeds during combat.  Even small groups like your own can benefit.  I'll travel with you for 300 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "All armies travelling in style bring a piper along to inspire them to heroic deeds during combat.  Even small groups like your own can benefit.  I'll travel with you for 300 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:47
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "You'll miss my inspiring battle tunes!  It makes a big difference during battle!"
msgstr "You'll miss my inspiring battle tunes!  It makes a big difference during battle!"

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:48
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npcprof.txt.py:48
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "All travel times reduced by one day (minimum of one day).  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."
msgstr "All travel times reduced by one day (minimum of one day).  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:48
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npcprof.txt.py:48
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "My experience in travelling the world can speed your journeys by a day whether you travel by land or by sea.  All I require is 100 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "My experience in travelling the world can speed your journeys by a day whether you travel by land or by sea.  All I require is 100 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:48
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "You don't find me useful?  Well, just remember that I save you time, and time is money!    "
msgstr "You don't find me useful?  Well, just remember that I save you time, and time is money!    "

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:49
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npcprof.txt.py:49
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "All boat travel reduced by two days, gold is increased by ten percent when found, and Reputation is decreased by one full category.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."
msgstr "All boat travel reduced by two days, gold is increased by ten percent when found, and Reputation is decreased by one full category.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:49
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npcprof.txt.py:49
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Arrr.  My life as a freedom-loving sailor has taught me to travel quickly on the seas and count my gold well.  But I'm down on my luck these days, so I'll sign on with you for only 500 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "Arrr.  My life as a freedom-loving sailor has taught me to travel quickly on the seas and count my gold well.  But I'm down on my luck these days, so I'll sign on with you for only 500 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:49
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Arrr.  Ye be firing this poor old sailor unjustly ye be.  Won't ye reconsider?"
msgstr "Arrr.  Ye be firing this poor old sailor unjustly ye be.  Won't ye reconsider?"

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:50
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npcprof.txt.py:50
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Armor and weapon skills are increased by two points for each character.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."
msgstr "Armor and weapon skills are increased by two points for each character.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:50
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npcprof.txt.py:50
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "All warriors need a squire to take care of their weapons and armor and back them up in battle.  I'll be your squire for 600 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "All warriors need a squire to take care of their weapons and armor and back them up in battle.  I'll be your squire for 600 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:51
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npcprof.txt.py:51
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Perception skill is increased by five points and Luck statistics are increased by ten points for each character.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."
msgstr "Perception skill is increased by five points and Luck statistics are increased by ten points for each character.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:51
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npcprof.txt.py:51
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Fortune is my business, and I can improve your fortunes for 400 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find.  "
msgstr "Fortune is my business, and I can improve your fortunes for 400 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find.  "

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:51
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "I predict you'll regret dismissing me!"
msgstr "I predict you'll regret dismissing me!"

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:52
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npcprof.txt.py:52
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Food use is reduced by one day's worth of food when resting (minimum one day), Merchant skill is increased by three points for each character, and Reputation is decreased by one full category.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."
msgstr "Food use is reduced by one day's worth of food when resting (minimum one day), Merchant skill is increased by three points for each character, and Reputation is decreased by one full category.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:52
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npcprof.txt.py:52
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "My entire life has been spent on the road, and believe me when I say you gotta know how to travel and you gotta know how to deal.  I can help you with both for 100 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "My entire life has been spent on the road, and believe me when I say you gotta know how to travel and you gotta know how to deal.  I can help you with both for 100 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:52
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "I cook your food and save you money, and this is the thanks I get?"
msgstr "I cook your food and save you money, and this is the thanks I get?"

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:53
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Your party is considered to have the most beneficial arrangement of races in any social situation while %01 is in your party.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."
msgstr "Your party is considered to have the most beneficial arrangement of races in any social situation while %01 is in your party.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:53
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npcprof.txt.py:53
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Not everyone knows how to talk strangers into giving them what they want.  I make it my specialty.  Bring me along and I'll use my skills to ease your way through society.  My rate is 500 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "Not everyone knows how to talk strangers into giving them what they want.  I make it my specialty.  Bring me along and I'll use my skills to ease your way through society.  My rate is 500 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:53
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:54
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Wait!  Let's talk about this!  I know you don't really want to dismiss me.  We can work it out!"
msgstr "Wait!  Let's talk about this!  I know you don't really want to dismiss me.  We can work it out!"

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:54
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npcprof.txt.py:54
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Merchant skill is increased by eight points for each character and Reputation is decreased by one full category.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."
msgstr "Merchant skill is increased by eight points for each character and Reputation is decreased by one full category.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:54
#: mm6/data/10LocLANG.icons/npcprof.txt.py:54
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Lots of people can be talked out of stuff they would never give up if they thought about it.  The trick is to talk fast and don't let them pause to consider what you're really saying.  I'll stay with you and coach you on this valuable skill for only 200 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "Lots of people can be talked out of stuff they would never give up if they thought about it.  The trick is to talk fast and don't let them pause to consider what you're really saying.  I'll stay with you and coach you on this valuable skill for only 200 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:55
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Disarm Traps and Stealing skills are increased by eight points for each character and Reputation is decreased by one full category.  %01 costs you nothing!"
msgstr "Disarm Traps and Stealing skills are increased by eight points for each character and Reputation is decreased by one full category.  %01 costs you nothing!"

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:55
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Need traps disarmed?  Perhaps something retrieved without the owner's knowledge or consent?  I've been doing it ever since I was released from jail three years ago.  If you need help, I'll come with you for free!  I need the practice.  "
msgstr "Need traps disarmed?  Perhaps something retrieved without the owner's knowledge or consent?  I've been doing it ever since I was released from jail three years ago.  If you need help, I'll come with you for free!  I need the practice.  "

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:55
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "What?  I didn't do nothin!  "
msgstr "What?  I didn't do nothin!  "

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:56
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Hour of Power"
msgstr "Hour of Power"

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:56
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Casts Hour of Power once per day for a duration of six hours.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."
msgstr "Casts Hour of Power once per day for a duration of six hours.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:56
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Few people outside of the Wizard's realm possess the knowledge to cast Hour of Power.  I can cast it once per day for your party if you'll hire me.  I only charge 2500 gold initially, and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "Few people outside of the Wizard's realm possess the knowledge to cast Hour of Power.  I can cast it once per day for your party if you'll hire me.  I only charge 2500 gold initially, and %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:56
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "You're would give up all the spells I cast on you for a few measly gold pieces?  Think it through carefully, my friend."
msgstr "You're would give up all the spells I cast on you for a few measly gold pieces?  Think it through carefully, my friend."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:57
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Two point bonus to Self (body, mind, spirit) spell skills for all characters.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."
msgstr "Two point bonus to Self (body, mind, spirit) spell skills for all characters.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:57
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "I can assist your spell casting by slightly boosting your spells of the Self for 500 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find.."
msgstr "I can assist your spell casting by slightly boosting your spells of the Self for 500 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find.."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:57
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:58
#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:59
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "By firing me, you're not just losing a friend and spiritual advisor, but your link to the Gods!  I know you don't really mean it.  You won't dismiss me."
msgstr "By firing me, you're not just losing a friend and spiritual advisor, but your link to the Gods!  I know you don't really mean it.  You won't dismiss me."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:58
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Initiate"
msgstr "Initiate"

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:58
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Three point bonus to Self (body, mind, spirit) spell skills for all characters.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."
msgstr "Three point bonus to Self (body, mind, spirit) spell skills for all characters.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:58
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "My prayers can magnify your Self spell skills for 1000 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "My prayers can magnify your Self spell skills for 1000 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:59
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Four point bonus to Self (body, mind, spirit) spell skills for all characters.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."
msgstr "Four point bonus to Self (body, mind, spirit) spell skills for all characters.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:59
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "I can greatly increase the effect of your Self spells for a small initial donation of of 2000 gold and then %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "I can greatly increase the effect of your Self spells for a small initial donation of of 2000 gold and then %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:60
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Monk"
msgstr "Monk"

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:60
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Increases the unarmed and dodging skills by two for all characters.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."
msgstr "Increases the unarmed and dodging skills by two for all characters.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:60
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "I can help train your minds and bodies to perfect your unarmored, unarmed combat techniques.  I only require 500 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "I can help train your minds and bodies to perfect your unarmored, unarmed combat techniques.  I only require 500 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:60
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "You, uh, haven't snatched the pebble from my hand yet, grasshopper.  Will you cut short your training so casually?"
msgstr "You, uh, haven't snatched the pebble from my hand yet, grasshopper.  Will you cut short your training so casually?"

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:61
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Increases the identify item and identify monster skills by six for all characters.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."
msgstr "Increases the identify item and identify monster skills by six for all characters.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:61
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "I have considerable knowledge of the items and creatures of Erathia.  I'd be willing to help you out in your travels for 750 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "I have considerable knowledge of the items and creatures of Erathia.  I'd be willing to help you out in your travels for 750 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:61
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "You will miss my excellent advice and knowledge the minute I am gone, mark my words!"
msgstr "You will miss my excellent advice and knowledge the minute I am gone, mark my words!"

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:62
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Hunter"
msgstr "Hunter"

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:62
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Increases the identify monster skill by four for all characters.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."
msgstr "Increases the identify monster skill by four for all characters.  %01 takes %17 percent of all gold you find."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:62
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "I've hunted most every type of creature in Erathia, and I know a little something about all of them.  Though I'm retired from hunting, I'll share my knowledge with you for 500 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."
msgstr "I've hunted most every type of creature in Erathia, and I know a little something about all of them.  Though I'm retired from hunting, I'll share my knowledge with you for 500 gold to start and %17 percent of the gold we find."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCPROF.TXT.py:62
msgctxt "npcprof"
msgid "Well, this old hunter knows not to beg.  Go on and dismiss me if you want."
msgstr "Well, this old hunter knows not to beg.  Go on and dismiss me if you want."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:2
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Emerald Island is southeast of Erathia, and far away from pirates and other ruffians.  It would be ideal, if not for the constant swarms of dragonflies that infest the island.  Fortunately, the large number of armed and skilled people this contest has attracted should thin their numbers a bit.\n\nLord Markham has supplemented the normally sparse village with a weapon, armor, and alchemist shop for your convenience during the contest.  A temple and basic magical guilds are also available.  I would suggest making sure that you are completely ready before you start off on the contest."
msgstr "Emerald Island is southeast of Erathia, and far away from pirates and other ruffians.  It would be ideal, if not for the constant swarms of dragonflies that infest the island.  Fortunately, the large number of armed and skilled people this contest has attracted should thin their numbers a bit.\n\nLord Markham has supplemented the normally sparse village with a weapon, armor, and alchemist shop for your convenience during the contest.  A temple and basic magical guilds are also available.  I would suggest making sure that you are completely ready before you start off on the contest."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:54
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You have decided that you no longer desire my information about the places on Emerald Island.  If you later decide that you'd like to hear what I have to say, then select Tour On."
msgstr "You have decided that you no longer desire my information about the places on Emerald Island.  If you later decide that you'd like to hear what I have to say, then select Tour On."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:190
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Priests.  You have come to me seeking that I be your guide on the Path of Light.  But be warned, to learn its ways, you must learn the ways of your own soul.  I would suggest that we meditate on this for awhile, but you look like you're in a hurry.  South of Bracada is an island called Evenmorn, and upon that island are the old temples of the Sun and the Moon.  Both are inhabited by the remnants of the two religions, their once proud churches reduced to two old temples fighting for a small island.\n\nThe Church of the Sun was the founding religion for our current faith, the Path of Light.  I propose we help them out and tip the balance in favor of the Church of the Sun.  Using the map that Daedalus Falk sent you to find in order to become priests, convince a sea captain to bring you to the island.  There, bring aid and comfort to the Church of the Sun by purifying the altar in the Church of the Moon.  This will so weaken the Moon cult that the Church of the Sun will be able to overcome them in battle.  Return to me when you have done this.   "
msgstr "Priests.  You have come to me seeking that I be your guide on the Path of Light.  But be warned, to learn its ways, you must learn the ways of your own soul.  I would suggest that we meditate on this for awhile, but you look like you're in a hurry.  South of Bracada is an island called Evenmorn, and upon that island are the old temples of the Sun and the Moon.  Both are inhabited by the remnants of the two religions, their once proud churches reduced to two old temples fighting for a small island.\n\nThe Church of the Sun was the founding religion for our current faith, the Path of Light.  I propose we help them out and tip the balance in favor of the Church of the Sun.  Using the map that Daedalus Falk sent you to find in order to become priests, convince a sea captain to bring you to the island.  There, bring aid and comfort to the Church of the Sun by purifying the altar in the Church of the Moon.  This will so weaken the Moon cult that the Church of the Sun will be able to overcome them in battle.  Return to me when you have done this.   "

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:199
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Priests.  [Falk gazes coldly at you] Well it is that you have come to see the wisdom of the Path of the Dark.  Never regret your decision, and never look back.  South of Bracada is an island called Evenmorn, and upon that island are the old temples of the Sun and the Moon.  Both are inhabited by the remnants of the two religions, their once proud churches reduced to two old temples fighting for a small island.\n\nThe Church of the Moon was the founding religion for our current faith, the Path of Darkness.  I propose we help them out and tip the balance in favor of the Church of the Moon.  Using the map that I sent you to find, convince a sea captain to bring you to the island.  There, bring aid and comfort to the Church of the Moon by defiling the altar in the Church of the Sun.  This will so weaken the Sun cult that the Church of the Moon will be able to overcome them in battle.  Return to me when you have done this.   "
msgstr "Priests.  [Falk gazes coldly at you] Well it is that you have come to see the wisdom of the Path of the Dark.  Never regret your decision, and never look back.  South of Bracada is an island called Evenmorn, and upon that island are the old temples of the Sun and the Moon.  Both are inhabited by the remnants of the two religions, their once proud churches reduced to two old temples fighting for a small island.\n\nThe Church of the Moon was the founding religion for our current faith, the Path of Darkness.  I propose we help them out and tip the balance in favor of the Church of the Moon.  Using the map that I sent you to find, convince a sea captain to bring you to the island.  There, bring aid and comfort to the Church of the Moon by defiling the altar in the Church of the Sun.  This will so weaken the Sun cult that the Church of the Moon will be able to overcome them in battle.  Return to me when you have done this.   "

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:207
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Welcome back, students.  The golem lesson was just an exercise, but to advance to Archmage, you really have to do something for the profession.  Copies of the fabled Divine Intervention spell are very rare, and unfortunately the School doesn't have one.  There's been a history of bad luck regarding the spell.\n\nIt has been around for time immemorial, but the spell has never found its way into our hands.  Always just out of reach, we often send guild members to find it, but every one has failed.  Sometimes they have it in their hands, but lose it on the way back, other times, the book seems to vanish, only to resurface 20 years later in some old dungeon, or on a deserted island.  Right now, we think it's in the Breeding Zone in the Pit.  Find the spell, and return with it.  Break the curse!"
msgstr "Welcome back, students.  The golem lesson was just an exercise, but to advance to Archmage, you really have to do something for the profession.  Copies of the fabled Divine Intervention spell are very rare, and unfortunately the School doesn't have one.  There's been a history of bad luck regarding the spell.\n\nIt has been around for time immemorial, but the spell has never found its way into our hands.  Always just out of reach, we often send guild members to find it, but every one has failed.  Sometimes they have it in their hands, but lose it on the way back, other times, the book seems to vanish, only to resurface 20 years later in some old dungeon, or on a deserted island.  Right now, we think it's in the Breeding Zone in the Pit.  Find the spell, and return with it.  Break the curse!"

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:212
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Fear not death?  I can perform the Ritual on any Wizard.  You need a Soul Jar.  Years ago the Wizards stole a shipment of Jars en route from Nighon to Deyja.  The jars are very hard to destroy, so they hid them, thinking we would never be able to find them.\n\nFortunately for us, dead men do indeed tell tales.  Better, in fact, than living ones--dead men never forget, never refuse to talk, and never lie.  So, we found the one who buried the Jars, and made him die.  He was very cooperative after his death, and said he hid them somewhere in the Walls of Mist for the Wizards in Celeste. \n\nRetrieve these jars and I will perform the Ritual on all Wizards amongst you.  The rest may become Honorary Liches, for what that's worth, in thanks for finding the extra Jars for us."
msgstr "Fear not death?  I can perform the Ritual on any Wizard.  You need a Soul Jar.  Years ago the Wizards stole a shipment of Jars en route from Nighon to Deyja.  The jars are very hard to destroy, so they hid them, thinking we would never be able to find them.\n\nFortunately for us, dead men do indeed tell tales.  Better, in fact, than living ones--dead men never forget, never refuse to talk, and never lie.  So, we found the one who buried the Jars, and made him die.  He was very cooperative after his death, and said he hid them somewhere in the Walls of Mist for the Wizards in Celeste. \n\nRetrieve these jars and I will perform the Ritual on all Wizards amongst you.  The rest may become Honorary Liches, for what that's worth, in thanks for finding the extra Jars for us."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:248
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Welcome back, Lords of Harmondale!  Now, I will help you.  My engineer will work for you.  Fix up your castle.  You have my thanks.  You are welcome here forever.\n\nHmmph.  One more thing.  Your work has interested the other courts.  They will send ambassadors to you now--check your throne room.  Watch your back, my friends."
msgstr "Welcome back, Lords of Harmondale!  Now, I will help you.  My engineer will work for you.  Fix up your castle.  You have my thanks.  You are welcome here forever.\n\nHmmph.  One more thing.  Your work has interested the other courts.  They will send ambassadors to you now--check your throne room.  Watch your back, my friends."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:264
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "[Queen Catherine inclines her head regally] You are the lot that won Lord Markham's silly contest, I see.  I must admit I had little faith until the Dwarf King recognized you as the rightful rulers of Harmondale.  You must have done something to win his respect, or he would have nothing to do with you.  I'm still not sure what he saw in you, but perhaps there really is something of substance here.  We shall see.\n\nMaybe you can do something for me that would make me think I should let you keep your new titles.  Recently, a valuable...agent of mine was arrested in the Tularean Forest for merely doing his job.  They're keeping him in a cave somewhere outside of Pierpont.  His name is Loren Steel, and they are threatening to execute him if certain unacceptable conditions are not met in 28 days.  Return with him before then and you will win respect, gold, and gratitude."
msgstr "[Queen Catherine inclines her head regally] You are the lot that won Lord Markham's silly contest, I see.  I must admit I had little faith until the Dwarf King recognized you as the rightful rulers of Harmondale.  You must have done something to win his respect, or he would have nothing to do with you.  I'm still not sure what he saw in you, but perhaps there really is something of substance here.  We shall see.\n\nMaybe you can do something for me that would make me think I should let you keep your new titles.  Recently, a valuable...agent of mine was arrested in the Tularean Forest for merely doing his job.  They're keeping him in a cave somewhere outside of Pierpont.  His name is Loren Steel, and they are threatening to execute him if certain unacceptable conditions are not met in 28 days.  Return with him before then and you will win respect, gold, and gratitude."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:315
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Our plans rapidly approach their conclusion, but there is a hitch.  The Kreegan--also known as the Devils, or the Demons, must be destroyed before we finish our plans.  They represent a terrible threat, and though they do little but lick their wounds today, will one day regain their strength and devastate the world.  If anything we do is to have lasting effect, we must first destroy these monsters for once and for all.\n\nYou are strong, but not strong enough to defeat the devils on your own.  They are vulnerable to the brand of magic most commonly wielded by the Necromancers, and less so by our own Wizards.  It is imperative that you infiltrate the Devil's base and kill their leader Xenofex.  That should end their threat to this world for some time.  The Warlocks have dug a tunnel from their volcano to the Land of the Giants-- the land the Devils claim as their own.  Perhaps you can use that."
msgstr "Our plans rapidly approach their conclusion, but there is a hitch.  The Kreegan--also known as the Devils, or the Demons, must be destroyed before we finish our plans.  They represent a terrible threat, and though they do little but lick their wounds today, will one day regain their strength and devastate the world.  If anything we do is to have lasting effect, we must first destroy these monsters for once and for all.\n\nYou are strong, but not strong enough to defeat the devils on your own.  They are vulnerable to the brand of magic most commonly wielded by the Necromancers, and less so by our own Wizards.  It is imperative that you infiltrate the Devil's base and kill their leader Xenofex.  That should end their threat to this world for some time.  The Warlocks have dug a tunnel from their volcano to the Land of the Giants-- the land the Devils claim as their own.  Perhaps you can use that."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:332
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Soon our plans will bear fruit, but there are a few details that must be handled before we are ready.  The Kreegan, also known as the Devils, share this world with us.  The only reason we're sharing is because they are weak right now.  If they ever get strong, they will try to kill every person in the world.\n\nAnyway, it's no fun to rule a world full of dead people, so we have to kill the Devils before they kill us.  Our plan is for you to infiltrate the Devils lair and destroy their leader, Xenofex.  The warlocks of Nighon have dug a tunnel from their volcano to the Land of the Giants-- the land of the Devils.  You can probably use that tunnel to get there."
msgstr "Soon our plans will bear fruit, but there are a few details that must be handled before we are ready.  The Kreegan, also known as the Devils, share this world with us.  The only reason we're sharing is because they are weak right now.  If they ever get strong, they will try to kill every person in the world.\n\nAnyway, it's no fun to rule a world full of dead people, so we have to kill the Devils before they kill us.  Our plan is for you to infiltrate the Devils lair and destroy their leader, Xenofex.  The warlocks of Nighon have dug a tunnel from their volcano to the Land of the Giants-- the land of the Devils.  You can probably use that tunnel to get there."

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:350
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "Our finest hour is upon us.  While you have been taking care of all those important tasks, my compatriots and I have been struggling with our former friends for the parts we need to rebuild the Heavenly Forge of legend.  By former friends, I mean the four chief advisors to King Magnus of the Wizards.  They have a plan to build a gate to the Ancients.  They could have stood with us, but threw it all away on some vague hope of a 'better future'.  But you!  You have stood with us all this time.\n\nOnly one task remains--we need the Oscillation Overthruster from our old vehicle, the Lincoln.  We have been unable to find one on your world.  The ship is in the sea west of Avlee and secured against entry, even from ourselves.  Now you must wear our environment suits, enter the ship, and return with the Overthruster.  Our old environments suits have been prepared for you in the chest outside this throne room.  For the suit to function properly you must not be wearing any equipment.We will stand watch over the Forge, and defend it against our enemies.  Bring us the Overthruster, my friends, and together, we shall rule the world!"
msgstr "Our finest hour is upon us.  While you have been taking care of all those important tasks, my compatriots and I have been struggling with our former friends for the parts we need to rebuild the Heavenly Forge of legend.  By former friends, I mean the four chief advisors to King Magnus of the Wizards.  They have a plan to build a gate to the Ancients.  They could have stood with us, but threw it all away on some vague hope of a 'better future'.  But you!  You have stood with us all this time.\n\nOnly one task remains--we need the Oscillation Overthruster from our old vehicle, the Lincoln.  We have been unable to find one on your world.  The ship is in the sea west of Avlee and secured against entry, even from ourselves.  Now you must wear our environment suits, enter the ship, and return with the Overthruster.  Our old environments suits have been prepared for you in the chest outside this throne room.  For the suit to function properly you must not be wearing any equipment.We will stand watch over the Forge, and defend it against our enemies.  Bring us the Overthruster, my friends, and together, we shall rule the world!"

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:356
msgctxt "npc conversation"
msgid "You need to have your own deck of cards to play. We will supply the opponent.  Victory conditions vary per inn. Build your tower, destroy your opponent's tower, or collect enough resources before your opponent does. \n\nLarge yellow numbers in column are the generators. This is how many new units of a particular resource you will receive on your next turn. Small black numbers in column are the resources. This is how many units you have available to spend on your current turn.\n\nCards: Each have their own cost to play, indicated in a small circle in the lower right corner of the card. The cost will be deducted from your resources according to the color of the card.  Left click on a card plays the card. Right click on a card to discard without playing.\n\nRed represents your Quarry Generator which produces your Brick resources, blue represents your Magic Generator which produces Gem resources, green represents your Zoo generator which produces Beast resources. \n"
msgstr "You need to have your own deck of cards to play. We will supply the opponent.  Victory conditions vary per inn. Build your tower, destroy your opponent's tower, or collect enough resources before your opponent does. \n\nLarge yellow numbers in column are the generators. This is how many new units of a particular resource you will receive on your next turn. Small black numbers in column are the resources. This is how many units you have available to spend on your current turn.\n\nCards: Each have their own cost to play, indicated in a small circle in the lower right corner of the card. The cost will be deducted from your resources according to the color of the card.  Left click on a card plays the card. Right click on a card to discard without playing.\n\nRed represents your Quarry Generator which produces your Brick resources, blue represents your Magic Generator which produces Gem resources, green represents your Zoo generator which produces Beast resources. \n"

#: mm7/DATA/10LocLANG.events/NPCTEXT.TXT.py:427
